language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Football squad: choose players within a budget of GBP 30 million (30000 in thousands) so that the total price is as large as possible, with position limits and a minimum squad size.
$ prices in GBP thousands of the players in order: goalkeepers g1-g3, defenders d1-d8, midfielders m1-m10, strikers s1-s5
letting price = [730, 1280, 3880, 920, 1310, 1620, 2410, 2790, 3280, 3910, 4570, 1800, 2630, 3170, 3769, 4140, 4750, 5380, 5930, 6780, 7130, 4460, 6470, 7780, 8390, 9500]
find buy : matrix indexed by [int(1..26)] of bool
find z : int(0..30000)

branching on [buy]
maximising z
such that
$ the total price of the chosen players is z, in GBP thousands
z = (sum i : int(1..26) . buy[i] * price[i]),
$ the chosen players must add up to no more than the upper limit of GBP 30 million
z <= 30000,
$ exactly one goalkeeper must be bought (players 1 to 3)
(sum i : int(1..3) . buy[i]) = 1,
$ at least two defenders must be bought (players 4 to 11)
(sum i : int(4..11) . buy[i]) >= 2,
$ at least three midfielders must be bought (players 12 to 21)
(sum i : int(12..21) . buy[i]) >= 3,
$ at least two strikers must be bought (players 22 to 26)
(sum i : int(22..26) . buy[i]) >= 2,
$ at least eleven players must be bought in total
(sum i : int(1..26) . buy[i]) >= 11
